The generator that produced Lemma 10.9's selector leaves.

  gen_assembly.py  the shape-theorem table: each schema's statement as the file proves it,
                   plus the 13-leaf map from (which-coordinate-is-i, which-is-j) to a schema
  final.py         the planner and leaf-body emitter (demand-driven: the body is generated
                   first, and disequalities/projections are emitted only when a step asks)
  wrapleaf.py      wraps one leaf as a standalone schema + a concrete instantiation at A_n,
                   which is what gives it a real verdict

Usage:
  python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'.'); import wrapleaf, final;
              print(wrapleaf.wrap(*list(final.LEAF)[0]))"

All 13 leaves verify strictly. Kept because the assembly is regenerable from it, and because
the four rounds of 'unused fact' it took to get right are recorded in CHAPTER10-PAINPOINTS.
